@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #F0F8FF
skinparam defaultFontColor #333333
skinparam arrowColor #666666
participant Client
participant "RPC Server" as RPC
participant "UTXO Store" as UTXO

Client -> RPC : reassign(oldtxid, oldvout, oldutxohash, newutxohash)
activate RPC
RPC -> RPC : Parse the three hexadecimal hashes\nCast oldvout to uint32
note right of RPC
  Short hashes are zero-padded.
  Negative indices are not rejected before the cast.
  Both full and limited RPC users can call this method.
end note
alt Hash parsing fails
  RPC --> Client : Error
else Hashes parsed
  RPC -> UTXO : ReAssignUTXO(old outpoint/commitment, new commitment)
  activate UTXO
  note right of UTXO
    Requires a frozen output.
    SQL does not check the old commitment.
    Aerospike checks the old commitment.
  end note
  alt Store operation fails
    UTXO --> RPC : Error
    RPC --> Client : Error
  else Store operation succeeds
    UTXO -> UTXO : Replace commitment, clear freeze, set maturity height
    UTXO --> RPC : Success
    RPC --> Client : JSON null
  end
  deactivate UTXO
end
note over Client, UTXO #FFDDDD
  Do not use ownership-changing reassignment.
  The replacement script is not persisted.
  Both owners remain unable to spend after maturity.
  Successful processing does not prove spendability.
  See the reassignment limitation in the Alert Service guide.
end note
deactivate RPC
@enduml
